  "title": "Democrats win largest House majority since 1992 after flipping North Carolina seat",
  "summary": "Democrats have secured their best general election result in decades, winning at least 258 seats in an election sweep unseen since 1992 that creates not only vast opportunities to govern but also intense pressure to deliver on campaign promises and priorities. Democrats have gained 44 House seats so far, four more than the 40 they picked up in President Donald Trump's first midterm in 2018.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Democrats have secured at least 258 seats in the House after winning four more midterm races.",
      "confidence": 0.95
